+// (j) The detection at the periphery layer's real size: a swapchain of 1040
+// x 1028 (two views), the cursor's box 11, 12 and 14 pixels (scales 0.33,
+// 0.38, 0.45 of the 32-texel image), drawn as such an image holds it
+// (filtered), moving 9 x 3 pixels a frame over the test world, eight
+// independent pairs each; the built-in arrow, and with XRFG_TEST_DCS_BIN (a
+// DCS bin directory) the game's own cursor images. Three ways:
+//  - "enlarged": the periphery layer's detection as round 8 has it (the
+//    image read enlarged 5 times, D3D12SmoothCursorOptions::small_sprite);
+//  - "plain": the unchanged detection on the same images (the control: it
+//    should find nothing);
+//  - "composed twin" (at 0.38 only: each run holds 5200 x 5140 images): the
+//    same frames enlarged 5 times on the CPU as Quad Views' composition
+//    enlarges the periphery, through the unchanged detection: what the
+//    composed mode sees.
+// Required: the enlarged detection judges every pair, and accepts as many
+// pairs as the composed twin does (the parent's criterion: not worse than
+// the composed mode); counted as a failed guess rather than stopping the
+// run. Everything is printed.
+void test_periphery_cursor_real_size(D3D12WarpFixture& fixture, xrfg::D3D12OpticalFlowBackend backend,
+    const xrfg::D3D12NvidiaOpticalFlowOptions& base) {
